## Q4. Difference Between Compiler and Interpreter

| Point           | Compiler                              | Interpreter                                   |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| Translation     | Translates the whole program at once  | Translates code line by line                  |
| Execution       | Executes after compilation            | Executes during translation                   |
| Error Detection | Shows errors after compiling          | Shows errors line by line                     |
| Speed           | Generally faster                      | Generally slower                              |
| Output          | Creates machine/object code           | Usually does not create separate machine code |
| Error Handling  | Multiple errors can be shown together | Stops when it finds an error                  |
| Examples        | C, C++                                | Python                                        |
| Process         | Compile → Run                         | Translate and Run                             |

